@startuml dsd_uc2_makeNewReturn_findSale
' NewEra POS - Design sequence diagram, UC2 Handle Returns: makeNewReturn() and findSale(receiptNumber) (Contracts 5 and 6), W11
' Team D - editable source of assets/dsd_uc2_makeNewReturn_findSale.png
' Render with: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng assets/dsd_uc2_makeNewReturn_findSale.puml
' Participants: logical view (architecture.md 4.2). Operations: system_interfaces.md 3.3, 3.7, 4.1 to 4.3; AD-05, AD-07, AD-08, AD-09.
' Messages marked <<new>> are not in the logical view or in system_interfaces.md yet (sent to Borja for the design class diagram).
title DSD UC2 Handle Returns - makeNewReturn() and findSale(receiptNumber) (Contracts 5 and 6)
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam defaultFontSize 11
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 6
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFBE6
skinparam NoteBorderColor #B7791F
skinparam maxMessageSize 190
hide footbox
box "ui.api" #EAF2E3
  participant "ctrl:ReturnController" as C
end box
box "application" #E8EEF7
  participant "h:ReturnHandler" as H
end box
box "domain" #FFF7E0
  participant "session:CashierSession" as CS
  participant "r:Return" as R
  participant "s:Sale" as S
end box
box "application.interfaces" #F6EDF7
  participant "repo:Transaction\nRepository" as TR
  participant "sync:StoreDatabase\nSync" as SY
end box

== makeNewReturn() (Contract 5) ==
[-> C : POST /api/returns
C -> H : makeNewReturn()
H -> TR : nextTransactionID()
TR --> H : id (e.g. R02-000154)
H -> CS : createReturn(id) <<new>>
CS -> R ** : create(id, session)
note right of R : isComplete = false\nlinked to the open CashierSession
CS --> H : r
H --> C : returnID
C -->[ : 201 return ID

== findSale(receiptNumber) (Contract 6) ==
[-> C : PUT /api/returns/{returnID}/sale {receiptNumber}
C -> H : findSale(receiptNumber)
H -> TR : find(receiptNumber)
note right of TR : the receipt number is the transaction ID (data_model.md);\nlocal copy first, so a sale of this register needs no network
alt found in the local copy
  TR --> H : s
else not in the local copy (sale made at another register)
  TR --> H : none
  H -> SY : findTransaction(receiptNumber)
  note right of SY : FR-21, AD-05: asked only when the local copy has no answer;\nthe store database is not on the path of a normal return
  alt NOT_FOUND, or the transaction is not a sale (4a)
    SY --> H : NOT_FOUND
    H --> C : SALE_NOT_FOUND
    C -->[ : 404 "No sale found with this receipt number" (NFR-14)
  else NOT_AVAILABLE (the store database does not answer)
    SY --> H : NOT_AVAILABLE
    H --> C : SALE_NOT_AVAILABLE <<new>>
    C -->[ : 409 "The sale is not in this register and the store database does not answer. Try again later."
  else FOUND
    SY --> H : s
  end
end
opt s found
  H -> S : isWithinRefundPeriod(today)
  note right of S : Information Expert: the sale knows its date;\nthe period is a setting, 30 days (BR-07)
  alt older than the refund period (5a)
    S --> H : false
    H --> C : OUT_OF_PERIOD
    C -->[ : 409 "This sale is older than the refund period"
  else within the period
    S --> H : true
    H -> TR : returnedQuantities(s.receiptNumber) <<new>>
    TR --> H : quantity already returned for each line
    note right of TR : returns of this register
    H -> SY : returnedQuantities(s.receiptNumber) <<new>>
    note right of SY : returns of the same sale at the other registers (FR-22); the adapter applies the timeout (AD-07)
    alt the store database answers
      SY --> H : quantity already returned for each line
      H -> H : keep the larger quantity of the two for each line
    else NOT_AVAILABLE
      SY --> H : NOT_AVAILABLE
      note over H, SY : Only the returns of this register are known: the risk of a second refund at another register is accepted, as for the overdue check of UC3 (detailed_design.md §7)
    end
    H -> R : setSale(s, returnedQuantities)
    H --> C : SaleView(lines, bought, already returned, tender)
    C -->[ : 200 lines of the sale with the quantity bought and already returned, and the tender
  end
end

note over H
  GRASP
  Controller: ReturnController only receives the request; ReturnHandler runs the use case (AD-01).
  Creator: CashierSession creates the Return it owns (it holds the open session), as for the Sale in UC1.
  Information Expert: Sale knows its date and says whether it is within the refund period.
  Indirection, Protected Variations: TransactionRepository and StoreDatabaseSync are interfaces (DC-02); the handler does not know which one answers.
  Low Coupling: the controller never calls the repository or the domain.
end note
@enduml
